Support MinGW-w64 GCC (MSYS2) as the host toolchain on Windows.

Upstream supports GCC/Clang hosts only on POSIX systems; on Windows the
build must be bootstrapped with Visual C++ or Open Watcom itself. This
patch teaches the build system and the small host-compatibility layer
about a GCC toolchain running on an NT host, so the whole tree can be
bootstrapped and built from MSYS2 with mingw-w64 GCC. The bootstrap tools
and the 64-bit Windows host tools (binnt64) are compiled by GCC; everything
else is built by the bootstrapped Open Watcom compilers as usual.

Build system:
 * build.sh, bld/wmake/posmake: recognise a MINGW/MSYS uname and build a
   native NT wmake.exe with the POSIX makefile.
 * bld/builder/preboot: use gcc for the builder tool on an NT host.
 * build/mif/cpuoscfg.mif, local.mif: allow bld_os=nt for GCC/CLANG, emit
   __NT__ instead of __UNIX__, use .dll, drop -gz (unsupported by the
   MinGW driver), don't redefine _M_X64/_M_IX86 which the mingw-w64
   headers provide, emit an import library next to every DLL (the
   makefiles expect it, as MSVC link produces one), and link the Win32
   import libraries MSVC treats as default libraries.
 * build/mif/exetarg.mif, dlltarg.mif: wrap libraries in a link group (GNU
   ld resolves archives in order, MSVC link does not, and the makefiles
   rely on that); skip 'chmod -x' on NT; strip the whole symbol table
   before wrc binds resources, which leaves stale COFF pointers otherwise.
 * build/mif/libtarg.mif: merge sub-libraries through an ar MRI script;
   GNU ar adds an archive as a plain member where MSVC lib merges it.
 * build/mif/cproj.mif: point wrc at the OW Win32 API headers, as the
   Watcom-hosted build does, instead of relying on a Windows SDK in
   INCLUDE.
 * bld/trap/*/ntx64.trp/makefile, bld/trap/ntx64.def: the trap DLL entry
   points are looked up by ordinal; use a .def file instead of MSVC
   -EXPORT options.
 * bld/wipfc/master.mif: wipfc needs C++11 (<cstdint>) under GCC/Clang.
 * bld/rcsdll, bld/ide/ide, bld/wv/utils/trap2txt: declare the C++
   projects as such so they link with g++ (MSVC cl does not care).

Host compatibility layer:
 * bld/watcom/h/clibext.h, bld/watcom/c/clibext.c: let __MINGW32__ share
   the MSVC (non-Watcom NT) branch, guarding the few macros and typedefs
   mingw-w64 already has; map the spawn* family to the underscored CRT
   versions whose prototypes match the callers; implement ultoa and cputs
   which MSVC gets from oldnames.lib and the UCRT only ships underscored.
 * bld/watcom/h/watcom.h: spell pointer_int as long long for non-MSVC
   64-bit Windows compilers (__int64 is only a macro after a CRT header).
 * bld/cc/h/cconst.h: GCC on Win64 predefines __SEH__ for its own
   unwinder; the C compiler uses the same name with a different meaning.
 * bld/f77/wfc/c/cptraps.c: FPE_* aliases, mingw-w64 float.h only has the
   underscored names.
 * bld/posix/src/compress/compress.h: sys/utime.h for MinGW as well.
 * bld/posix/src/env/env.c, bld/mstools/*/c/*.c: include clibext.h where
   spawn* is called without it.
 * bld/wmake/c/mexec.c: don't split the command word at '+', which
   truncated 'g++' to 'g' when wmake spawns the compiler directly.

Source fixes GCC insists on:
 * bld/sdk/fmedit, bld/sdk/wde, bld/dig: token pasting of a name onto a
   parenthesised argument list or a string literal ('x##(', '## c',
   'xstr(a)##xstr(b)') is not valid C; MSVC and Watcom tolerate it.
 * bld/sdk/imgedit: EnumChildWindows callbacks declared with LONG instead
   of LPARAM, which differ in width on Win64.
 * bld/ide/ide: WString converts to both const char* and long, making
   two WCheckBox/WPushButton constructors ambiguous; cast at the call.
 * bld/wclass/hpp/wfile.hpp: include <stdio.h> for SEEK_SET.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

diff --git a/bld/builder/preboot b/bld/builder/preboot
index 2bed2e9c..aaf5a5f1 100644
--- a/bld/builder/preboot
+++ b/bld/builder/preboot
@@ -23,7 +23,13 @@ cc_opts_nt    = -bcl=nt
 cc_opts_linux = -bcl=linux
 CL = *wcl386 -zq $(cc_opts_$(bld_os)) -fe=$(name_exe)
 !else ifdef __NT__
+! ifdef __GCC_TOOLS__
+CL = gcc -g -O2 -o$(name_exe)
+! else ifdef __CLANG_TOOLS__
+CL = clang -g -O2 -o$(name_exe)
+! else
 CL = cl /nologo /Fe:$(name_exe)
+! endif
 !else
 CL = cc -g -O2 -o$(name_exe)
 !endif
